# agent tooling: per-session scratch. The 01-oss rule layer itself IS tracked, and
# the reason is not that /oss:scaffold regenerates it -- being regenerated is no
# argument for committing anything. It is that a fresh git worktree takes its rule
# layer from git, and this repo's maintenance loop cuts one worktree per issue, so
# untracking the layer would silently disable it for every delegated agent. It is
# inert for anyone without the plugin that reads it -- CONTRIBUTING.md says so and
# tests/test_agent_layer.py holds it to that (#2). Only this state directory is
# per-session and per-machine.
.claude/jit-context/.discovery/

# uv lockfile. Requivo is a library: its dependency floors and ceilings are the
# contract, declared in pyproject.toml. A lock here would pin what a consumer
# resolves against and is not what a library ships.
uv.lock
